    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25789" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lānĭfĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		lana-facio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>wool-working, that works in wool</i>, i. e. <i>spinning, weaving</i>, etc. (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					2, 1, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Claud. in Eutr. 2, 382</span></i>:
			sorores, <i>the spinning sisters</i>, i. e. <i>the Fates</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 6,
				58, 7</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Juv. 12,
			66</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lānĭfĭca</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a
			wool-spinner</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 7, 12, § 5
		sq.</span></i></div>
